      "content": "I understand your concerns, but 800 mg every 6 hours is the recommended dose for severe pain and inflammation. If you're worried about stomach issues, you can take an antacid along with the ibuprofen. And as for the bleeding risk, ibuprofen can increase the risk, but it's generally considered safe in moderate doses. Just make sure to monitor your blood pressure and watch for any signs of bleeding, like unusual bruising or blood in your urine or stool. If you experience any of these symptoms, stop taking the ibuprofen and call a doctor immediately. But if you're feeling good and your blood pressure is stable, you can continue taking the 800 mg every 6 hours. Remember, I'm here to help you feel better, so don't hesitate to ask if you need more advice.",
